course: dictionary
lesson: 7867
title: Keeping dry with a raincoat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A raincoat is a waterproof coat that you wear to keep dry when it rains. When you read a word like raincoat, look at the words around it to help you. «The weather can change during the day, so a jumper or raincoat is packed when the forecast says so.» The forecast says rain, so a raincoat is something you bring to stay dry.
explain: Read the whole sentence and ask: what would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence. «A boy in Dublin sees sunshine in the morning but the forecast says showers later, so he packs a raincoat and a jumper.» Showers are rain, so a raincoat must be for rain, and the boy stays warm and dry on the way home.
explain: Notice how a word can be used in other ways. «The Rhino took off his skin, which buttoned underneath and looked like a waterproof» is a story, and the waterproof is the author's comparison to a raincoat. The word waterproof tells you what matters: water cannot get through it.
fact: A raincoat is a waterproof coat that you wear to keep dry in the rain.
fact: «Waterproof» means water cannot get through.
fact: Raincoats are made from waterproof materials, which is why scientists test which materials keep water out.
fact: Related words for raincoat include anorak, mac, rain jacket and wellies (rain boots).
fact: «Mac» is an informal word for a raincoat, and wellies are rubber boots for wet days.
exercise: «The weather can change during the day, so a jumper or raincoat is packed when the forecast says so.» What is a raincoat? | A bag for carrying wet towels | A coat that keeps water out, so you stay dry in the rain | A hat that shades you from the sun | *A coat that keeps you warm in the snow
exercise: «A boy in Dublin sees sunshine in the morning but the forecast says showers later, so he packs a raincoat and a jumper.» Why does the boy pack a raincoat? | A swimming towel | To look smart at school | *To stay dry when the showers come | Sunglasses
exercise: What does waterproof mean? | Made of wood | Very warm to wear | Full of holes | *Water cannot get through it
test: Which word is a related word for raincoat? | Football | Teapot | Sunhat | *Anorak
test: «Plastics are useful everywhere, from hospitals to raincoats.» What must the material of a raincoat be? | *Waterproof | Sandy | Sticky | Thirsty
exam: Mum says, «Wear your raincoat, it's raining.» Why does she say this? | *So you will stay dry in the rain | Because the raincoat is new and shiny | Because it is sunny and hot | Because raincoats make you taller
